# ThreadSanitizer suppressions: uninstrumented third-party libraries only.
#
# Qt, glib, libdbus and libstdc++ ship uninstrumented, so the happens-before
# edges they establish (the QDBusConnection thread's handoff in particular) are
# invisible to TSan, and every object one of them allocates on one thread and
# frees on another reads as a race between its own new and its own delete. The
# fix would be instrumented builds of those libraries, which no distribution
# ships; the suite builds against the packaged ones.
#
# `called_from_lib` suppresses TSan's INTERCEPTORS when the named library is the
# immediate caller. A race in Dish's own code, or in an interceptor Dish calls,
# still reports. Never a `race:` pattern, and never a first-party library.

# QObject, QThread and the event loop: cross-thread deleteLater and the
# queued-connection handoffs.
called_from_lib:libQt6Core.so
# The QDBusConnection thread that the screen-saver inhibit, the BlueZ probe,
# logind and the Secret Service calls run on.
called_from_lib:libQt6DBus.so
# The HTTP thread QNetworkAccessManager runs the manifest and controller
# database fetches on.
called_from_lib:libQt6Network.so
# Qt 6.9 reimplemented QWaitCondition over std::condition_variable, so a Qt
# thread handoff enters the interceptor through libstdc++'s out-of-line
# condition_variable::wait instead of a libQt6* frame, and the lines above no
# longer match: TSan then reports "unlock of an unlocked mutex" against a mutex
# inside Qt-allocated memory it never saw locked (seen from
# QNetworkAccessManager's worker startup under test_moonlight_binding_refcount).
# It would hide a first-party std::condition_variable wait the same way, and no
# first-party code waits on one (SpeakerPlayoutEngine's queue moved to
# WorkerWake, a semaphore whose atomics TSan sees): grep src/ for
# condition_variable before keeping this line.
called_from_lib:libstdc++.so
# Qt's event dispatcher on Linux is glib's main loop; its sources and the
# GMainContext lock are taken from both the GUI and the D-Bus threads.
called_from_lib:libglib-2.0.so
# GObject's type registry, which glib's dispatcher initialises from whichever
# thread first touches it.
called_from_lib:libgobject-2.0.so
# libdbus, under QtDBus: its connection lock and message refcounts cross the
# D-Bus thread and the caller's.
called_from_lib:libdbus-1.so
